00:35:50,070 --> 00:35:53,610
in individuals who are
seronegative for Epstein

492
00:35:53,610 --> 00:35:57,430
-Barr virus. mTOR inhibitors,
sirolimus, and avirolimus

493
00:35:57,430 --> 00:36:06,910
bind FKBP12, and then
complex with mTOR, which

494
00:36:07,550 --> 00:36:11,930
inhibits that whole
cytokine signaling pathway,

495
00:36:12,830 --> 00:36:18,770
causing cell cycle
arrest in the G1 phase.

496
00:36:18,770 --> 00:36:21,530
It prevents G1 progression
to the S phase.

497
00:36:23,010 --> 00:36:26,190
And that inhibits T
cell proliferation and

498
00:36:26,190 --> 00:36:28,570
everything else that
goes on in that pathway.

499
00:36:29,530 --> 00:36:32,090
They are frequently
used in multi-drug

500
00:36:32,090 --> 00:36:34,350
regimens to allow
reduction of calcineurin

501
00:36:34,350 --> 00:36:37,010
inhibitors. mTOR inhibitors
are associated with

502
00:36:37,010 --> 00:36:39,110
impaired wound healing,
wound dehiscence,

503
00:36:39,210 --> 00:36:41,470
leukopenia,
saromocytopenia, anemia,

504
00:36:41,470 --> 00:36:44,010
hypercholesterolemia,
hypertriglyceridemia,

505
00:36:44,110 --> 00:36:47,570
diarrhea, peripheral
edema, and so on.

506
00:36:47,570 --> 00:36:52,170
Substrates of CYP3A4P
glycoprotein, low

507
00:36:52,170 --> 00:36:55,310
bioavailability, extensive
hepatic metabolism,

508
00:36:55,450 --> 00:36:57,870
high potential for
drug interactions.

509
00:36:59,070 --> 00:37:05,030
And here is a chart kind
of summarizing everything.

510
00:37:07,130 --> 00:37:10,370
And I thank you for
listening to this lecture.